{"qid": "hotpotqa:76096cce081ab5b9ef72be19076ee0a79d9e9239474e8b73", "question": "When did the place in Canada where François Beaucourt (1740-1794) was mainly active acquired its present name?", "answers": ["1763"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the evidence retrieved, François Beaucourt (1740–1794) was mainly active in the **Province of Quebec**[1][3].\n\nThe Province of Quebec acquired its present name through the **Royal Proclamation of 1763**, when the territory formerly known as Canada (the former French colony) was renamed the **Province of Quebec** following the British conquest during the Seven Years' War[5].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 34988.9, "error": ""}
