{"qid": "hotpotqa:c47c8d3b1917f017cafaecbb4cddd6b92171854247957c08", "question": "Who was born first,  Morgan Llywelyn or Robert Jordan?", "answers": ["Morgan Llywelyn"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Morgan Llywelyn** was born first.\n\n- **Morgan Llywelyn** was born on **December 3, 1937**[1].\n- **Robert Jordan** (born James Oliver Rigney Jr.) was born on **October 17, 1948**[7].\n\nMorgan Llywelyn was born about 11 years before Robert Jordan.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 18036.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:f536646dd72a8a4f5ebddec61a67b8319dc9187d47bb7fc6", "question": "The winner of the the London Riders' Championship in 1953 scored how many points in the 1952 Individual Speedway World Championship?", "answers": ["14"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "The winner of the **London Riders' Championship in 1953** was **Jack Young**[1].\n\nRegarding his points in the **1952 Individual Speedway World Championship**, the search results did not return his specific 1952 score. The retrieved data shows that in the **1953** Individual Speedway World Championship, Jack Young finished 5th with **10 points**[4], but the question asks about **1952**.\n\nBased on the available evidence, Jack Young scored **10 points** in a World Championship Final — however, the results I was able to retrieve only confirm this figure for the 1953 Final, not the 1952 Final. If you'd like, I can attempt a further search specifically about the 1952 World Championship results.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 48481.3, "error": ""}
