{"qid": "hotpotqa:3e4cce5082e968aec7f0c008b1acbd111f505d0579d1c9ee", "question": "Why did the CEO of the football team based in Denver, Colorado step down in 2014?", "answers": ["due to the onset and progression of Alzheimer's disease"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The CEO of the Denver Broncos, Pat Bowlen, stepped down in July 2014 due to the onset and progression of Alzheimer's disease[9]. Bowlen had served as the team's CEO since 1984, and his stepping down resulted in team president Joe Ellis and general manager John Elway assuming control of the team[3].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 17946.3, "error": ""}
