{"qid": "hotpotqa:a93aa642fb8802a99b36cd62febe1c4e995096a9320b00c5", "question": "Henry Roth and Lewis Mumford are both this nationality?", "answers": ["American"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Henry Roth and Lewis Mumford are both American nationals.\n\nHenry Roth was born in Tykocin, Russian Empire (now Poland) in 1906, brought to the United States in 1914, and became a United States citizen in 1915[1]. He was an American writer known for works like \"Call It Sleep\" and \"An American Type\"[3][5].\n\nLewis Mumford was born in Flushing, Queens, New York City in 1895 and was an American writer, philosopher, and social critic[6][7][9][10]. He was described as an \"American writer and philosopher\" who spent some time studying in England but remained an American national throughout his life.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 22013.9, "error": ""}
