{"qid": "hotpotqa:4d6aafffd109cb61fd543f44bda770fda0cf1e1c3798548b", "question": "1956 Night Series Cup games were played at what inner suburb of Melbourne that is 3km south of Melbourne's central business district?", "answers": ["Albert Park"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The 1956 Night Series Cup games were played at the **Lake Oval, Albert Park**. Albert Park is an inner suburb of Melbourne located approximately 3km south of Melbourne's central business district[1]. It was the home ground of South Melbourne and was the only ground equipped to host night games at that time[1][2].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 33573.9, "error": ""}
