{"qid": "hotpotqa:781060824875cb0343a110f5e6f83d46e638cbb89e2ad7c6", "question": "The FIBT World Championships 1960 took place in a town located in which part of Italy ?", "answers": ["the Veneto region of Northern Italy"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The FIBT World Championships 1960 took place in **Cortina d'Ampezzo**, which is located in **northern Italy**. Specifically, it is a town in the Province of Belluno, in the **Veneto region**, situated in the heart of the southern (Dolomitic) Alps[1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 18634.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:e8ba4badc3c5d30cc0942ede8df86a72257c492c07025dab", "question": "In modern history of Syria this kingdom lasted for only four months, this kingdom surrendered to who?", "answers": ["French"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "## Answer\n\nThe **Arab Kingdom of Syria** lasted only a little over four months, from **8 March to 25 July 1920**. The kingdom **surrendered to French forces** on 25 July 1920[1].\n\nThe kingdom was led by **Faisal bin Hussein** (son of Sharif Hussein bin Ali), who proclaimed it on 8 March 1920. Despite claiming territory over Greater Syria, Faisal's government controlled only a limited area and was ultimately unable to resist the French military intervention[1][5].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 16278.6, "error": ""}
