{"qid": "musique:a9233be5f19b456544331e69848af8bbf56256ce9ed0da78", "question": "In what region of the country of S-Fone is The place of birth of John Phan located?", "answers": ["South Central Coast"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "I now have enough information to answer the question. Let me piece together the facts:\n\n1. **John Phan** was born in **Da Nang, Vietnam**[1].\n2. **S-Fone** is a mobile communication operator in **Vietnam** — not a country, but a Vietnamese telecom company founded in Ho Chi Minh City[8]. Its CDMA network was launched in several cities including **Da Nang**, Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City, Hai Phong, and Can Tho[6].\n\nDa Nang is located in **Central Vietnam** (the central region of the country of Vietnam). Since S-Fone operated within Vietnam and Da Nang falls within its network coverage area, the answer is:\n\n**Da Nang is located in the Central region of Vietnam** (the country where S-Fone operated). S-Fone launched its services in Da Nang as part of its CDMA 2000 1x EV-DO rollout in 2006[6].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 55327.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:102eaee0943270c43f63b7d45a0088f6a8515e51a126d925", "question": "Along with the Closer performer, what notable pop artist started out his career on adult contemporary radio?", "answers": ["Michael Bublé"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Michael Bolton** is a notable pop artist who started out his career on adult contemporary radio, along with **Josh Groban** (the performer of the album *Closer*). Both artists had early success on AC radio before becoming major pop figures[1][2].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 65750.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:74528b7f4e2b5d4c1667751615829ad5e7dfd81f9eb55e0c", "question": "Who is the child of Sigrid Eskilsdotter's child?", "answers": ["Svante Stensson Sture"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the evidence retrieved, the answer is:\n\n**King Gustav Vasa (Gustav I of Sweden)**\n\nThe knowledge base clearly shows the family relationship:\n- **Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banér)** was the mother of **Christina Gyllenstierna**[1][3][5]\n- Sigrid was the **maternal grandmother of King Gustav Vasa of Sweden**[3]\n\nThe text confirms that after Sigrid returned to Sweden in 1523, \"her grandson was now king\"[5], referring to Gustav Vasa, who was the child of Christina Gyllenstierna.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 25538.5, "error": ""}
