{"qid": "musique:0942aa56c94ac545c00849686583273efd664347084e9682", "question": "Who led the muslim forces to retake the proposed embassy destination?", "answers": ["Abu Ubaidah"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved information, the Muslim forces that retook the proposed embassy destination were led by **Mawdud** (likely referring to Mu'izz al-Din Mawdud, the Seljuk atabeg of Mosul) [4]. The proposed embassy destination could correspond to any of the several taifa states mentioned in the results, such as Tortosa [1], Carmona [2], or Tavira [5], or possibly the fortress of Kushla [3]. However, the specific link between the \"proposed embassy destination\" and the retaking by Mawdud’s forces is not explicitly detailed in the available snippets.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 37048.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:8267f95a2928cb63203d20da0079d98138d4f58281fc4e9e", "question": "When did the party who gained control of congress in the midterm elections in 1946 take control of the determiner of rules of the US House and US Senate?", "answers": ["January 2015"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the wiki navigation results, I can provide the answer from general historical knowledge about the 1946 midterm elections and the structure of Congress.\n\n## Answer\n\nThe **Republican Party** gained control of both chambers of Congress in the **1946 midterm elections** (held on November 5, 1946). They took control of the congressional rules-determining bodies — the **House Rules Committee** and the **Senate Committee on Rules and Administration** — when the **80th United States Congress** convened on **January 3, 1947**.\n\nThis was the date on which the newly elected Republican majorities formally assumed control of all congressional committees, including those that set the rules of procedure for each chamber. This marked a significant shift in power, as Republicans had been in the minority since the early 1930s during the New Deal era.\n\n**Key details:**\n- **Election date:** November 5, 1946\n- **Party that gained control:** Republican Party\n- **Date of taking control:** January 3, 1947 (start of the 80th Congress)\n- **What they controlled:** House Rules Committee and Senate Rules Committee (the bodies that determine the rules of procedure for each chamber)", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 32316.1, "error": ""}
