{"qid": "hotpotqa:105e7f4d337799315ddf870acc4ff2a62a1e6cdf489086cd", "question": "Gary L. Bennett was a part of the space missions that have a primary destination of what celestial body?", "answers": ["Sun"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Gary L. Bennett worked on the Voyager, Galileo, and Ulysses space missions. The Voyager and Galileo missions both had Jupiter as a primary destination, while Ulysses primarily studied the Sun[2][8]. The most consistent primary destination among the missions he contributed to is Jupiter.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 43178.1, "error": ""}
