{"qid": "hotpotqa:11a7ad9d646184c16480376226d58f1b2754b095563c8344", "question": "Thirukkalacherry is a village in which Indian town?", "answers": ["Tharangambadi"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, **Thirukkalacherry** (also spelled Thirukkalachery) is a small village in **Mayiladuthurai District**, Tranquebar (Tharangambadi) Taluk, Tamil Nadu, India[1]. The nearest town to the village is **Porayar**, which connects it to other major towns such as Karaikal, Mayiladuthurai, Sirkali, Nagapattinam, and Tiruchirappalli[2].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 21684.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:f039fe9cc81a0a312f9899beca2fe26b710bf8c3aa23a4d9", "question": "After Russell D. Moore served at the Southern Baptist Theological Seminary he became the President of The Ethics & Religious Liberty Commission (ERLC) in what year?", "answers": ["2013"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Russell D. Moore became President of the Ethics & Religious Liberty Commission (ERLC) on **June 1, 2013**[1]. This was after his prior service at the Southern Baptist Theological Seminary, where he served as dean of the School of Theology, senior vice president for academic administration, and professor of theology and ethics[2].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 28020.1, "error": ""}
