{"qid": "hotpotqa:de85aaa5c535ba20bdcad5fbabfe13a03687374265a57b44", "question": "Were the Tundra Mine and Negus Mine located in the same country?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Yes, the **Tundra Mine** and the **Negus Mine** were located in the **same country — Canada**. Both operated in the **Northwest Territories** of Canada[3][6]. Specifically:\n\n- **Tundra Mine** was a gold mine in the Northwest Territories, Canada, operating from 1962 to 1968[3].\n- **Negus Mine** was a gold producer at Yellowknife, Northwest Territories, Canada, operating from 1939 to 1952[6].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 17775.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:87fd3f0590498461d595ff1823632c79b66cf313cf55fbb3", "question": "Are Yoo-hoo and Faygo both carbonated drinks?", "answers": ["no"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on my research, **not both** Yoo-hoo and Faygo are carbonated drinks:\n\n- **Faygo** is indeed a carbonated soft drink brand (a soda)[3][4].\n- **Yoo-hoo**, however, is **not carbonated**. It is an American brand of **chocolate-flavored beverage** made from water, high-fructose corn syrup, and whey[8]. It was created as a pasteurized chocolate drink in 1928[11].\n\nSo no — while Faygo is a carbonated soda, Yoo-hoo is a non-carbonated chocolate-flavored beverage.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 82692.7, "error": ""}
