{"qid": "hotpotqa:0a44085d7963681015a69416470b86da02135ac722d6301b", "question": "Jolyon James performed the role of Moonshadow in a musical by a composer of what nationality?", "answers": ["British"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Jolyon James performed the role of Moonshadow in the musical **Moonshadow**, which was composed by **Cat Stevens** (born Yusuf Islam). Cat Stevens is **British** — he was born in London, England, and is described as a British singer-songwriter and musician[3].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 9088.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:f1c0b9a9ec47ccda8ba4b1be0ca7083b961ba0f06b2a4df7", "question": "What Nobel Laureate teaches at  Chapman University?", "answers": ["Vernon Smith"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The Nobel Laureate who teaches at Chapman University is **Vernon L. Smith**[12][13].\n\nHe is a professor of business economics and law at Chapman University and co-winner of the **2002 Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences** (shared with Daniel Kahneman) for his contributions to behavioral economics and his pioneering work in **experimental economics**[13]. He is also the founder of the **Economic Science Institute** and the **Smith Institute for Political Economy and Philosophy** at Chapman University[12].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 46105.1, "error": ""}
