{"qid": "hotpotqa:1d81e1f410acc77f1d9a844f811045c2cecb0fdc9e717d41", "question": "Which filmmaker was known for animation, Lev Yilmaz or Pamela B. Green?", "answers": ["Levni Yilmaz"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Lev Yilmaz** is the filmmaker known for animation. He is an American independent filmmaker, artist, and publisher, best known for his **\"Tales of Mere Existence\" animated comic series**[12].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 48702.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:a16ac581bde4459861c8681858b07f82363f66142beed4c2", "question": "1920 Politics was a Republican political strategy to reassert the authority of the white race in which US state?", "answers": ["Hawaii"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the knowledge base, the **1920 Politics** was a Republican political strategy in **Hawaii**. After the previous \"Divide-and-Control\" strategy failed, Republicans adopted the \"1920 Politics\" approach to prevent majority rule by Americanizing the Japanese and Filipino communities—disconnecting them from their own cultural identities and pushing them to adopt a Western identity—thereby furthering the power of the white population[1][5].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 34288.2, "error": ""}
