{"qid": "hotpotqa:4636487a1855382398fe1e54284cb7dd3d7b8d178ac4a476", "question": "Migene González-Wippler is leading expert on a religion that developed among which ethnic group ?", "answers": ["West African descendants"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Migene González-Wippler is a leading expert on **Santería**, a religion that developed among **Afro-Cuban communities** following the Atlantic slave trade of the 16th to 19th centuries[2]. The religion formed through the blending of traditional religions brought to Cuba by enslaved West Africans—primarily **Yoruba**—with Roman Catholicism[2].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 18607.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:fbd2e6218ec7c8fc1a90b05bf6858a15d376704a278fa79f", "question": "Who was born first, Juan Rulfo or John le Carré?", "answers": ["Juan Rulfo"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "<tool_call>\n<function=knowledge_base_search>\n<parameter=query>John le Carré birth year</parameter>\n<parameter=knowledge_base_ids>[\"01a013b266d37561a1d82d8e32faf017\"]</parameter>\n<parameter=top_k>3</parameter>\n<parameter=multihop>False</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 29344.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:795ed5382ff9378f90123aedc2b638c049411295c5678466", "question": "Are Tantrix and Personal Preference both types of games?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "**Yes, both Tantrix and Personal Preference are types of games.**\n\n- **Personal Preference** is a 1987 board game created by Donal Carlston, in which players guess the order in which another player ranks foods, activities, people, and other items by preference. It was published by Broderbund, Playtoy Industries, and Parker Brothers International[9][10].\n\n- **Tantrix** is a tile-based puzzle/game that involves connecting tiles (referred to as \"Serpentiles\" in some contexts) into various configurations[1][3][7].\n\nSo yes, both are games, though they are quite different in nature: Personal Preference is a social/party board game, while Tantrix is a tile-based puzzle game.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 63668.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:7528b0be35e8e6007f07c98b9f2d45ee1c854298134aba5c", "question": "Sarah Price and Rob Schneider are both what profession? ", "answers": ["director"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the evidence retrieved:\n\n- **Sarah Price** is an American **filmmaker**, director, and producer, known for the documentary *American Movie* (1999), which won the Grand Jury Prize for Documentary at the Sundance Film Festival. She is a member of the Directors Guild of America[11].\n\n- **Rob Schneider** is an actor and comedian known for his work in film, television, and *Saturday Night Live*[6][7][8].\n\nBoth Sarah Price and Rob Schneider are **filmmakers** (film industry professionals) — Sarah Price as a director/producer of documentaries, and Rob Schneider as an actor and comedian in film and television.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 63607.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:1fd7df3ba224e985f87e976c7a4a67ddc1012a249a542bea", "question": "Hardley Flood is an area of lagoons that support populations of the waterfowl that are a medium sized version of what animal?", "answers": ["duck"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the knowledge base results, Hardley Flood supports populations of the **Common pochard** (*Aythya ferina*), which is described as a **medium-sized diving duck**[3][7]. So the waterfowl found at Hardley Flood are a medium-sized version of a **duck**.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 61946.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:3faa54c1f192293c709684aa60c6e2e8cfe34ff55c8b6248", "question": "Which is a shrub, Mimosa or Cryptocoryne?", "answers": ["Mimosa"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Mimosa** is the shrub. Mimosa is a genus of plants in the family Fabaceae (legumes), and many species within the genus grow as shrubs or small trees[1][2].\n\nIn contrast, **Cryptocoryne** is a genus of **aquatic/herbaceous plants** from the family Araceae, commonly found in streams, rivers, and flooded forest pools in tropical regions of India, Southeast Asia, and New Guinea[7]. It is not a shrub at all.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 44073.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:a18c0ece7c2ae88d2f9f3ffc5eaa13297a1b5d0125a172ad", "question": "Carlos Salazar Lomelín is the CEO of which Mexican multinational beverage retailer?", "answers": ["Fomento Económico Mexicano"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Carlos Salazar Lomelín is the CEO of **Coca-Cola FEMSA**. He has served as chief executive officer of the company since January 1, 2000. Coca-Cola FEMSA is a Mexican multinational beverage retailer, the largest bottler of Coca-Cola products in Latin America[4].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 25891.3, "error": ""}
