{"qid": "hotpotqa:90caafc7fe51eee4143874971f67bb3e0107d26179c437f7", "question": "Broadbent Arena and Freedom Hall are landmarks of which U.S. city?", "answers": ["Louisville"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Broadbent Arena and Freedom Hall are landmarks of **Louisville, Kentucky**[4][7]. Both venues are located on the grounds of the Kentucky Exposition Center in the city.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 31097.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:8fddd32ef1d88a5f8fde49152fc015eb80b3d60d1108d073", "question": "What side-scrolling platform game had Christian Whitehead as project lead?", "answers": ["Sonic Mania"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The side-scrolling platform game that had Christian \"Taxman\" Whitehead as project lead was **Sonic Mania**[1][3][4]. Developed in 2017 in collaboration with Headcannon and PagodaWest Games, it was an original title in the Sonic the Hedgehog series. Development began in 2015, led by Whitehead, who was a prominent member of the Sonic fangame community and had previously been contracted by Sega to develop remastered ports of earlier Sonic games for mobile devices[3][4].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 31963.3, "error": ""}
