{"qid": "hotpotqa:4cdf613f05eaa834f5867ee486ec94d47587f09b5a7bb6db", "question": "What is the character of fictional character Claire Fraser in a British-American television drama series developed by Ronald D. Moore ?", "answers": ["Claire is a married World War II nurse"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "## Claire Fraser in *Outlander*\n\n**Outlander** is a British-American historical drama television series developed by **Ronald D. Moore**, based on Diana Gabaldon's novel series, and it premiered on Starz on August 9, 2014.\n\n**Claire Fraser** (also known as Claire Beauchamp/Randall) is a fictional character portrayed by **Caitríona Balfe**. Her character is described as follows:\n\n- **Background**: She is a **married former World War II nurse** (later a surgeon) who, in 1945, finds herself mysteriously transported back in time to **Scotland in 1743**.\n- **Personality**: She is described as **smart, stubborn, and willful**. She uses her wits, practical medical skills, and knowledge of the future to survive in the 18th century.\n- **Story Arc**: In the past, she meets and falls in love with **Jamie Fraser** (Sam Heughan), a dashing Highland warrior and tacksman of Clan Fraser of Lovat. She marries him and becomes embroiled in the **Jacobite rising**.\n- **Surnames**: She adopts the surnames **Randall**, **Fraser**, and **Grey** at various points throughout the series[1][3][4].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 15175.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:bf8ee342564ae21a17b169023f83a20220a63198827a0232", "question": "The Panel with striding lion  was one of many that lined the way north of the gate to the inner city of what location?", "answers": ["Babylon"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The Panel with striding lion was one of many that lined the Processional Way north of the Ishtar Gate, which led to the inner city of **Babylon**[1][5].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 16446.5, "error": ""}
