{"qid": "hotpotqa:b524574cca42824f963480aae00867719108113389d087d3", "question": "What river does Waterloo Bridge and London Eye have in common?", "answers": ["Thames"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Waterloo Bridge and London Eye both have the **River Thames** in common.\n\n- **Waterloo Bridge** is a road and foot traffic bridge **crossing the River Thames** in London[4].\n- **The London Eye** is an observation wheel located on the **South Bank of the River Thames** in London[9].\n\nBoth landmarks are situated along the Thames, with Waterloo Bridge spanning it and the London Eye standing on its south bank.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 27665.8, "error": ""}
