{"qid": "musique:220004b7b3836d023f1e416666c0d8d43ae75a77c1a8bdd0", "question": "Who was the first African American student at the university Robert Khayat was educated at?", "answers": ["James Howard Meredith", "James Meredith"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Robert Khayat was educated at the **University of Mississippi** (Ole Miss), where he earned both bachelor of arts and Juris Doctor degrees[5]. The first African American student at the University of Mississippi was **James Meredith**, who became the first African-American student to enroll there on October 1, 1962[8][10]. His admission was a pivotal moment in the civil rights movement, sparking the Ole Miss riot of 1962.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 19700.9, "error": ""}
