{"qid": "musique:8cad76dd1dfee0d4847e99f55e46c401a1087fde2aee2cc8", "question": "Who did the person considered the founder of three major monotheistic religions marry after the death of Sarah?", "answers": ["Keturah"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the knowledge base evidence, the person considered the founder of the three major monotheistic religions (Judaism, Christianity, and Islam) is **Abraham** (also known as Ibrahim in Arabic).\n\nAccording to the Book of Genesis, **Abraham married Keturah** after the death of his first wife, Sarah[1][2]. Abraham and Keturah had six sons together.\n\nIt is worth noting that according to Jewish tradition, some commentators (notably Rashi) believed Keturah was the same person as Hagar, whom Abraham had previously married and then remarried after her return[2]. However, this identification is generally rejected by modern scholars, who view Keturah and Hagar as two different individuals[2].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 108058.5, "error": ""}
