{"qid": "musique:ede452592bbb410b3678e75fc6aaaeeda204fffc69034041", "question": "When did Burroughs Corporation merge to form a new corporation?", "answers": ["1986"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Burroughs Corporation merged with Sperry in **1986** to form **Unisys**. The merger was valued at $4.8 billion, with Burroughs buying Sperry. The name \"Unisys\" was chosen from over 31,000 submissions in an internal competition, combining parts of the words \"united,\" \"information,\" and \"systems.\" At the time, this was the largest merger in the computer industry, creating the second-largest computer company with annual revenue of $10.5 billion.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 14092.8, "error": ""}
